        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-18T15:44:39.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Related question about the consistency of playing cards on other cards: The cards that get played on other cards aren't consistent in their wording as to how they get played on other cards. They are self-consistent within one keyword class, but not across keywords. Is there any functional difference between playing a card \"next to\" another card (e.g. a Bounty) and playing a card \"in front of\" another card (e.g. a Link)? For instance...if a target has two Bounties \"next to\" it on its left and right, respectively, as well as one Link \"in front of\" it, Visionary can still play Twist the Ether on it, yes?</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:13:45.921Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 1,
