        "read": false,
        "user_title": "",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Related question about the consistency of playing cards on other cards: The cards that get played on other cards aren&#39;t consistent in their wording as to how they get played on other cards. They are self-consistent within one keyword class, but not across keywords. Is there any functional difference between playing a card &quot;next to&quot; another card (e.g. a Bounty) and playing a card &quot;in front of&quot; another card (e.g. a Link)? For instance...if a target has two Bounties &quot;next to&quot; it on its left and right, respectively, as well as one Link &quot;in front of&quot; it, Visionary can still play Twist the Ether on it, yes?</p>",
